WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.730
I have 1,000 and only want to lose 20. So I just put it all in?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.151
What's in your account, how much you buy in this trade,

00:00:12.151 --> 00:00:16.425
and the most you plan to lose are three different things. Decide your exit first.

00:00:16.425 --> 00:00:18.060
Then you can size the position.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.880
One practice sum. Entry at 50,000, planned exit at 47,500. That's 5% away.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:46.890
If you plan to take a 20 price loss, ignoring costs, the position is about 400.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.250
So 'lose at most 20' doesn't mean 'buy only 20'?

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:16.330
Right. Here a 400 position falling 5% is the 20. These are teaching numbers only.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.628
Real markets have slippage, gaps, fees and failed orders,

00:01:38.628 --> 00:01:41.532
so planned risk is not a guaranteed maximum loss.

00:01:41.532 --> 00:01:43.607
Never borrow money for this course,

00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:46.570
and never practise with money you need to live on.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:56.680
Twenty.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.113
Work out the worst you can accept first.

00:01:59.113 --> 00:02:01.460
Then ask whether you need this trade at all.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.407
You set a stop-loss. Does that mean you can only lose that amount?

00:02:15.407 --> 00:02:17.170
Next: the truth about stops.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.850
Understand first, then act.
